WEBVTT

00:07.800 --> 00:09.900
The patient disappeared while in transport!

00:11.110 --> 00:14.130
Is this the monument?

00:15.310 --> 00:18.070
You're not from Neotopia, are ya?

00:19.010 --> 00:22.850
Gale, you've changed. What is it?

00:23.520 --> 00:25.090
Nothing at all.

00:25.090 --> 00:27.050
I'm just disappointed in you.

00:27.620 --> 00:29.680
He's living with us now.

00:30.190 --> 00:32.760
We are taking you into custody.

00:32.760 --> 00:35.960
In the name of Absolute Justice,
I now punish you.

00:35.960 --> 00:39.660
Stop it!

00:40.870 --> 00:48.610
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

00:48.610 --> 00:55.570
Tooku tooi basho e to

01:08.930 --> 01:15.140
Kaze ni fukare aruite yuku

01:15.140 --> 01:22.100
Umarekita imi o shiritakute

01:22.310 --> 01:28.620
Tatoeba ushinau toki ga kitemo

01:28.620 --> 01:35.750
Dakishimeru koto ima, erabou

01:38.190 --> 01:45.600
Bokutachi wa mina kitto te o nobashiterun da

01:45.600 --> 01:51.570
Nakusenai mono ni mukatte

01:51.570 --> 01:59.210
Kagayaita yume dake o taguriyosenagara

01:59.210 --> 02:06.090
Tooku tooi basho e to

02:32.450 --> 02:36.080
Episode 6
A Rushed Conclusion

02:39.150 --> 02:41.180
Why... Why?

02:41.620 --> 02:43.590
How could you?!

02:46.160 --> 02:47.330
Take him away.

02:47.330 --> 02:48.960
Sir!

02:55.600 --> 02:57.400
Come with me!

02:58.270 --> 02:58.910
Stop!

02:58.910 --> 03:00.180
After him!
Stop!

03:00.180 --> 03:02.040
It's no use!

03:02.040 --> 03:03.040
You won't make it.

03:03.040 --> 03:04.510
B..But...

03:04.510 --> 03:06.080
Calm down!

03:06.080 --> 03:08.450
I can more or less guess where they've gone.

03:17.290 --> 03:19.230
It's okay now.

03:19.230 --> 03:21.460
No one will find us here.

03:23.460 --> 03:25.430
Not Gale or anyone.

03:28.470 --> 03:30.100
Carter...

03:30.870 --> 03:33.930
I can't believe something like
that happened to Carter.

03:35.040 --> 03:39.810
He used to treat me like I was his own daughter.

03:41.150 --> 03:42.780
Damn it...

03:43.690 --> 03:47.560
Gale was never like that in the old days.

03:47.560 --> 03:50.060
No, he hasn't changed.

03:50.060 --> 03:52.650
This just means that he's one of
the adults of this country!

03:54.100 --> 03:55.500
Keith?

03:55.500 --> 03:57.800
It's perfectly clear to me now.

03:57.800 --> 03:59.770
I'm not wrong.

03:59.770 --> 04:02.830
It's this country that's in the wrong!

04:08.010 --> 04:12.850
The capital has authorized us to use this
assembly hall as our base of operations.

04:12.850 --> 04:15.850
And regarding the investigation
into the park's construction...

04:15.850 --> 04:17.320
What did you find out?

04:17.320 --> 04:20.420
No application has been submitted.

04:20.420 --> 04:22.060
I see...

04:22.060 --> 04:24.330
Reinforcements will also be here soon.

04:24.330 --> 04:27.560
You are to remain in command of the whole force.

04:27.560 --> 04:29.360
Very well.

04:30.060 --> 04:32.900
I guess this ruins your long-awaited vacation.

04:32.900 --> 04:36.100
No, on the contrary I am delighted,

04:36.100 --> 04:39.370
because I am now able to be of
service to my country.

04:42.240 --> 04:44.040
Please drink this.

04:44.910 --> 04:46.550
I'm sorry.

04:46.550 --> 04:49.450
It's my fault Carter was...

04:53.090 --> 04:55.290
You've done nothing wrong.

04:55.290 --> 04:57.260
We're the ones who are at fault.

04:57.260 --> 05:02.130
We wanted you to stay with us,
and we delayed in giving notice.

05:02.130 --> 05:06.500
But why would they kill Carter,
just because of that?

05:06.500 --> 05:08.630
And Gale is his...

05:09.840 --> 05:14.110
Carter willingly accepted his punishment,

05:14.110 --> 05:17.210
because that was the right thing to do.

05:17.210 --> 05:21.410
Carter and Gale both did as our
country teaches us.

05:26.490 --> 05:28.960
Go to Gale, Noah.

05:28.960 --> 05:32.450
Neotopia will take care of you.

05:43.240 --> 05:45.910
There is no problem with building a park.

05:45.910 --> 05:48.640
But you leveled this land and built this
park of your own accord,

05:48.640 --> 05:51.350
without submitting an application
to the government.

05:51.350 --> 05:56.680
You have effectively pillaged public land,
and that is a serious crime!

05:59.490 --> 06:05.160
You will all be relocated to various towns
and villages of our choosing.

06:05.160 --> 06:06.960
You have three days.

06:06.960 --> 06:10.470
Use the time to make your moving preparations.

06:10.470 --> 06:11.900
This is terrible!

06:11.900 --> 06:14.000
You mean we're all going to be split up?

06:14.000 --> 06:16.200
Are they going to level the
whole village or something?

06:22.010 --> 06:26.410
This judgment is not solely due to
your construction of the park.

06:26.410 --> 06:30.110
It is also in part for neglecting to report
the unidentified individual.

06:31.020 --> 06:35.110
If anyone spots the escaped youth,
you will notify us immediately.

06:35.960 --> 06:39.950
It will be your duty and honor
as citizens of Neotopia!

06:46.170 --> 06:49.070
This is happening to Ratt all because of me?

06:49.840 --> 06:51.040
You've got it wrong.

06:51.040 --> 06:52.840
How so?

06:53.140 --> 06:56.110
If disgruntled people are allowed
to be together for too long,

06:56.110 --> 06:58.340
it's only a matter of time before they erupt.

06:59.950 --> 07:03.620
But what you're saying is pure conjecture.

07:03.620 --> 07:05.390
That they'd do this on just a suspicion...

07:05.390 --> 07:07.410
That's how this country is.

07:08.190 --> 07:10.160
That's Neotopia...

07:18.070 --> 07:20.440
Why are you wrecking it?

07:20.440 --> 07:22.900
Everyone worked so hard to build it!

07:23.540 --> 07:25.170
Listen...

07:25.170 --> 07:30.010
It's only natural, since we built
that park against the law.

07:30.010 --> 07:32.240
We're the ones at fault.

07:41.020 --> 07:43.290
The soldiers are keeping a close eye
on everyone out there.

07:43.290 --> 07:46.060
It was nearly impossible just to get here.

07:46.060 --> 07:47.530
Who are these guys?

07:47.530 --> 07:48.830
Comrades.

07:48.830 --> 07:52.000
They are all skeptical of the
way this country is run.

07:52.000 --> 07:56.500
With things the way they've turned out,
we can't afford to hesitate any longer!

07:56.500 --> 07:58.130
Keith!

08:06.250 --> 08:08.250
These are...

08:08.250 --> 08:12.950
Long ago, our village performed a
great service to the country,

08:12.950 --> 08:14.580
in the war.

08:17.020 --> 08:19.290
The country praised the people's deeds,

08:19.290 --> 08:22.260
and took care of everything in their daily lives.

08:22.260 --> 08:24.030
In exchange for this,

08:24.030 --> 08:26.120
all the weapons were sealed away.

08:27.900 --> 08:31.270
I stumbled upon them just by chance.

08:31.270 --> 08:33.900
So, that's why you were on the lookout
for me when I came up here.

08:34.610 --> 08:35.940
That's right.

08:35.940 --> 08:39.000
Penalties for breaking the law
being extreme, as they are.

08:44.450 --> 08:46.920
Will you fight with those?

08:49.490 --> 08:51.960
There must be another way.

08:51.960 --> 08:53.900
Fighting isn't the way.

08:53.900 --> 08:55.860
You mustn't do it!

09:01.240 --> 09:06.470
The wind has been blowing the whole time,
I just didn't realize.

09:07.640 --> 09:10.270
The wind is blowing, Noah.

09:11.410 --> 09:13.040
Keith...

09:13.850 --> 09:15.980
It can't be stopped now.

09:22.860 --> 09:25.090
Why have things turned out like this?

09:25.990 --> 09:28.360
What's going to happen to Ratt?

09:29.330 --> 09:30.960
Aisha...

09:39.640 --> 09:42.280
Coming here of your own free will?

09:42.280 --> 09:44.510
Why the change of heart?

09:46.210 --> 09:48.520
How could you let Noah go?!

09:48.520 --> 09:52.190
Well, Noah and I, we want to protect Ratt!

09:52.190 --> 09:55.160
Do you have any idea what's
going to happen to him?!

09:57.090 --> 09:59.790
The country will be sure to take care of him.

09:59.790 --> 10:01.760
Like hell they will!

10:03.900 --> 10:06.830
You talk like everything's the government's fault.

10:06.830 --> 10:09.060
And now you want to fight them?

10:10.400 --> 10:12.310
Aisha...

10:12.310 --> 10:15.400
You've changed too, just like Gale!

10:18.780 --> 10:21.520
You want me to leave Ratt be?

10:21.520 --> 10:24.420
Listen to this nonsense!

10:24.420 --> 10:26.490
I am to blame.

10:26.490 --> 10:30.620
It's absurd that Ratt should vanish
because of me coming here!

10:31.160 --> 10:32.730
Don't get the wrong idea.

10:32.730 --> 10:37.330
The problem is that the people who live
here are in contempt of the law.

10:37.330 --> 10:39.430
It's just a minor offense!

10:39.430 --> 10:43.630
Why should Carter have to die for that?

10:50.580 --> 10:53.050
Stop pushing your luck!

10:53.050 --> 10:55.220
The only reason I am not
punishing you for fleeing

10:55.220 --> 10:58.880
is because the capital will judge whether or
not you have come from another world!

10:59.390 --> 11:02.120
Under any other circumstances,
I'd waste no time in...

11:03.090 --> 11:05.430
I don't care what happens to me.

11:05.430 --> 11:07.220
So please, spare Ratt.

11:21.340 --> 11:24.110
Out of the way, I've got to save Noah!

11:27.480 --> 11:28.750
You must understand.

11:28.750 --> 11:31.780
We can't take any further risks.

11:41.030 --> 11:42.830
I'm begging you.

11:43.960 --> 11:47.200
I'd like you to leave Ratt intact.

12:11.830 --> 12:14.490
I tried to persuade Gale, but...

12:15.330 --> 12:16.730
I'm sorry, Noah.

12:16.730 --> 12:20.690
But I'm sure there's another way to save Ratt.

12:21.740 --> 12:23.360
Yes...

12:26.240 --> 12:28.040
Run, Noah!

12:28.940 --> 12:30.570
Hurry!

12:32.910 --> 12:33.450
Stop!

12:33.450 --> 12:34.820
Aisha!
Stop!

12:34.820 --> 12:36.680
Why you...

12:36.680 --> 12:38.320
I want to speak with you!

12:38.320 --> 12:39.320
Hear me out.

12:39.320 --> 12:41.290
You can do that, can't you?

12:53.370 --> 12:55.340
What should I do?

12:57.240 --> 13:00.210
How can I save Ratt?

13:00.670 --> 13:02.470
How do I...

13:09.080 --> 13:12.250
Let's get out of Ratt before the
military comes in force.

13:12.250 --> 13:15.960
Now that Noah has surrendered, they aren't
conducting searches anymore.

13:15.960 --> 13:18.120
You guys can just go on your own.

13:19.090 --> 13:21.290
I'm going to save Noah.

13:22.160 --> 13:24.700
Noah will be taken to the capital in any event.

13:24.700 --> 13:27.870
We'll go to the capital, and join up
with the Resistance.

13:27.870 --> 13:31.140
If we fight here, we'll only die in vain!

13:31.140 --> 13:32.940
What about Ratt?

13:35.910 --> 13:38.040
There's no way to save Ratt.

13:39.980 --> 13:41.950
And you're okay with that?

13:51.390 --> 13:53.290
What the could it be?

13:53.290 --> 13:55.290
Are we under attack?

13:57.230 --> 13:59.330
Why here?

13:59.330 --> 14:01.470
Could Noah have told them?

14:01.470 --> 14:03.570
Noah's not that kind of guy!

14:03.570 --> 14:05.840
This is no time for arguing!

14:05.840 --> 14:07.540
What do we do, Keith?

14:07.540 --> 14:10.850
The only thing awaiting us is punishment,

14:10.850 --> 14:12.810
whether we wait here or not!

14:15.280 --> 14:17.080
Come out quietly.

14:17.080 --> 14:20.650
If you don't, that place will be your grave!

14:22.620 --> 14:24.530
Get out of here; I'll take care of him!

14:24.530 --> 14:26.150
Right!

14:26.990 --> 14:28.620
Gale!

14:46.550 --> 14:48.020
It's no use.

14:48.020 --> 14:50.280
They won't save themselves just by fighting.

14:51.990 --> 14:53.950
That won't work!

15:15.310 --> 15:19.350
Fool, you cannot begin to comprehend the
noble ideals of Neotopia's knights!

15:19.350 --> 15:21.320
I sure as hell don't understand what
kind of ideals you have,

15:21.320 --> 15:24.390
punishing people over the slightest offense
and destroying your hometown!

15:24.390 --> 15:26.620
It's called Absolute Justice!

15:26.620 --> 15:28.860
Observance of strict laws

15:28.860 --> 15:32.160
is precisely what will enable us to achieve the
greatest happiness for all citizens!

15:58.690 --> 16:01.220
You kill your own father and say you're happy?

16:01.220 --> 16:04.220
Quiet! I am just.

16:04.220 --> 16:06.220
I will punish you!

16:07.430 --> 16:09.260
Stop!

16:09.260 --> 16:10.890
Aisha?

16:12.770 --> 16:14.670
This isn't what you promised.

16:14.670 --> 16:16.660
You weren't going to kill Keith.

16:17.770 --> 16:19.830
What are you talking about, Aisha?

16:21.480 --> 16:23.340
I love Ratt.

16:23.340 --> 16:27.510
That's why I sought desperately
for a way to save it.

16:27.510 --> 16:29.820
Is this the answer?!

16:29.820 --> 16:32.190
Gale made a promise to me.

16:32.190 --> 16:37.320
He said he'd spare Ratt and that
he wouldn't punish you!

16:37.320 --> 16:38.660
You trusted him?

16:38.660 --> 16:39.660
You believed what he said?

16:39.660 --> 16:41.500
Well, it's Gale!

16:41.500 --> 16:43.900
Our childhood friend, Gale!

16:43.900 --> 16:46.670
Look at how close we were.

16:46.670 --> 16:48.970
We used to play together all the time.

16:48.970 --> 16:51.810
We loved each other so much!

16:51.810 --> 16:54.170
I love this village.

16:54.170 --> 16:56.810
I love how things used to be between us.

16:56.810 --> 17:00.350
Let's go back to being how we were.

17:00.350 --> 17:02.380
For that we need to have Ratt.

17:02.380 --> 17:04.120
You understand, don't you?

17:04.120 --> 17:06.450
So, don't take Ratt away from us.

17:07.690 --> 17:11.890
That is the kind of selfish thinking
that would destroy our country.

17:11.890 --> 17:16.230
Your actions are beyond despicable, therefore...

17:16.730 --> 17:18.530
I will punish you!

17:18.900 --> 17:20.530
Gale?!

17:25.340 --> 17:26.970
Aisha!

17:40.450 --> 17:42.080
Gale...

17:45.530 --> 17:46.660
How could you.. .

17:46.660 --> 17:49.160
How could you do that to Aisha?!

17:49.160 --> 17:50.330
It's her just rewards!

17:50.330 --> 17:53.730
The woman sold out your comrades
to satisfy her own desires!

17:53.730 --> 17:55.400
You bastard!

17:56.270 --> 17:58.510
Why do you rebel against our country's ideals?!

17:58.510 --> 18:00.410
Why don't you understand?!

18:00.410 --> 18:04.780
Your country's heartless " ideals" don't
mean a damn thing to me!

18:22.460 --> 18:24.000
Why?

18:24.000 --> 18:26.030
Why is this?

18:26.030 --> 18:28.000
Why is this?

18:52.930 --> 18:54.550
Noah!

19:00.600 --> 19:02.070
Is this...

19:02.070 --> 19:03.870
Did I do this?

19:06.270 --> 19:07.980
Noah...

19:07.980 --> 19:09.600
Aisha?

19:12.080 --> 19:13.710
Noah...

19:17.350 --> 19:20.180
You must not stay here.

19:22.460 --> 19:24.890
Could you prop me up?

19:28.330 --> 19:32.030
Even though I do have the power of shifting,

19:32.030 --> 19:34.400
I can't specify a destination.

19:35.470 --> 19:37.040
I'm sorry, Noah.

19:37.040 --> 19:39.170
Aisha!

19:39.170 --> 19:40.800
Noah...

19:42.140 --> 19:43.940
Live.

19:46.280 --> 19:50.780
If you survive, I know you'll make it back to Calm.

19:50.780 --> 19:52.750
Come with me, Aisha!

19:55.290 --> 19:58.060
This is my home here,

19:58.060 --> 20:00.030
my beloved village of Ratt.

20:02.460 --> 20:04.590
Farewell, Noah.

20:13.110 --> 20:15.900
Keith... Gale...

20:17.140 --> 20:21.550
I wish we could've been together forever.

20:45.870 --> 20:49.810
The power only to hurt others...

20:49.810 --> 20:52.970
Keith... Aisha...

20:58.920 --> 21:01.220
Grandpa! Someone's collapsed here!

21:02.490 --> 21:05.520
I'm surprised we'd encounter another
person here of all places.

21:12.600 --> 21:16.170
How long do you plan to take
care of this young man?

21:16.170 --> 21:20.010
We are a people who do not
associate with outsiders.

21:20.010 --> 21:23.540
Is that not the law of our clan?

21:23.540 --> 21:27.580
I could not leave a man half-dead
in the wilderness.

21:27.580 --> 21:30.580
That's right, we can't do that!

21:30.580 --> 21:33.190
Yet, we must also abide by the law.

21:33.190 --> 21:35.810
The law benefits both sides too, you know.

21:36.920 --> 21:41.700
Nevertheless, we cannot just throw him
out into this raging sandstorm.

21:41.700 --> 21:47.660
Let us postpone our decision until
the storm has abated.

21:59.610 --> 22:06.020
I believe I've said that I have an interest
in the spirit that resides in you.

22:06.020 --> 22:08.990
Would you hurry up and bring it out to fight?

22:08.990 --> 22:11.660
Otherwise, the spectators will all go home on us,

22:11.660 --> 22:13.920
since this match is so boring.

22:50.400 --> 22:54.270
Kimi no sono kokoro no naka o nozoite
shiritai sono kimochi to hyoujou

22:54.270 --> 22:58.170
Hitori seotta kimi no sugata kirari
hikaru namida no wake wa

22:58.170 --> 23:01.740
Kikazu ni iwazu ni okuru yo eeru
sagashiteru kotae no aida ni

23:01.740 --> 23:05.870
Kodawarisugizu kangaesugizu asu
no kimi ni komorebi kanjiru

23:07.580 --> 23:09.420
Very very much de ii kanji

23:09.420 --> 23:11.220
Very very good kimi to boku

23:11.220 --> 23:15.090
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai to omotterun da

23:15.090 --> 23:16.920
Very very much itsudatte

23:16.920 --> 23:18.760
Very very good kawaranai

23:18.760 --> 23:24.720
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

23:30.240 --> 23:32.710
Mayoi no naka kono yasashisa kanji

23:34.010 --> 23:36.480
Donna toki mo kimi o zutto shinji

23:37.740 --> 23:41.650
Koko ni ookiku hirogaru keshiki
buruusukai no hi no shita de

23:41.650 --> 23:45.780
li kibun ii mibun ii jibun zutto koko ni itai kibun

23:47.250 --> 23:49.060
Very very much de ii kanji

23:49.060 --> 23:50.890
Very very good kimi to boku

23:50.890 --> 23:54.690
ltsudemo kimi no soba ni ite
agetai toomotterun da

23:54.690 --> 23:56.560
Very very much itsudatte

23:56.560 --> 23:58.430
Very very good kawaranai

23:58.430 --> 24:04.390
Bokura wa itsumo kibou de
chikarazuyoku saiterun da (Oh)

24:16.750 --> 24:19.990
Next Time
Awakened Feelings

24:17.020 --> 24:19.990


